extraction_notes: |
  - Underseas, printed 37-38. The book heads the race "Rurlel Eel People" and
    its skill list "Rurlel Warrior R.C.C. Skills"; the Experience Tables on
    printed 214 call the class "Rurlel Eelman", and that is the stored name,
    per the book-survey rule that the authority table wins. All three readings
    are here so the choice is checkable.
  - PRINTED 37 IS HEAVILY OVERPRINTED WITH ARTWORK and its OCR is interleaved
    with illustration noise. The attribute, size, weight, M.D.C., horror factor
    and natural-ability lines were RE-READ off a 200 dpi render of that page
    rather than trusted from the cache. The render agreed with the cache on
    every value.
  - THE SECONDARY-SKILL SHAPE IS BACKWARDS FROM THE USUAL and is transcribed as
    printed. Printed 38 gives the Rurlel no secondary skills at first level and
    one each at levels two, four, eight and twelve. Most classes here start
    with several and gain more; this one starts with none. Stored as count 0
    with that schedule.
  - MEDICAL IS STORED NARROWER THAN THE BOOK PRINTS IT. Printed 38 allows any
    Medical skill and gives +10% to Sea Holistic Medicine only. A category
    entry carries ONE bonus that applies to every skill in it, so granting the
    category with +10% would hand the bonus to every medical skill. The row
    grants Sea Holistic Medicine at +10% via `only`, which loses the rest of
    the Medical category. The narrower reading was chosen because it is the
    half the book singles out, and because an over-granted bonus is silent
    where a missing option is visible.
  - MECHANICAL IS BASIC MECHANICS ALONE, and the catalog spells it that way.
    Checked against `SELECT name FROM skills WHERE category = ''Mechanical''`
    on production before storing it, because an `only` naming a row that does
    not exist fails CLOSED - it grants nothing and says nothing.
  - PILOT IS RESTRICTED TO THREE ROWS. Printed 38 allows power armour, if
    designed for their body, plus water scooters and water skiing and surfing.
    Stored as an `only` list. The "if designed to accommodate their body and
    needs" condition is a GM call and is not modelled.
  - THE MAGIC-USING 10% ARE NOT A VARIANT. Printed 38 says one Rurlel in ten is
    an ocean mage built as an Ocean Wizard O.C.C. instead. That is a different
    class rather than a stage of this one, so it is a restriction line pointing
    at `ocean-wizard` rather than a `variants` block.
  - Speed is the SWIMMING speed, which is the only one the book gives. The
    Rurlel is a 25 foot eel and the book states no land speed at all.
  - THE ROLL-WITH-IMPACT BONUS IS STORED UNDER `roll`, NOT `roll_with_impact`.
    The first draft of this class used the longer name, which parses,
    validates, composes and renders NOWHERE - `sheet.js` draws a literal
    COMBAT_FIELDS list and `roll` is the key in it. Checked against that list
    rather than guessed.
