# Rurlel Eelman

## Lore

The Rurlel, pronounced *rule el*, are a warrior race of D-bees who have made their home off the coast of Chile and Peru in the Pacific Ocean. Although they venture into the depths, they are accustomed to the comparatively shallow water of the continental shelf, where sea life is abundant. They hunt fish, crustaceans and invertebrates, grow and eat seaweed, and keep fisheries where they cultivate their own aquatic livestock.

They are a simple people who enjoy life and respect the ocean, living in harmony with its natural ecology and trying to avoid contact or trouble with surface dwellers. They are aloof and casual toward other aquatic beings too, preferring to keep to themselves in quiet little communities along the coast. Except for the occasional adventurer, explorer or rogue, the eelmen have never allied themselves with any group.

The upper torso is humanoid and roughly human sized; the rest is eel, running to twenty-five feet from head to tail tip.

## GM Notes

The Rurlel fight only to defend themselves and their people. They count the stidjron, the minions of the Lord of the Deep, and sea monsters among their enemies, and are indifferent toward everyone else. As hunters and warriors they are accomplished enough to be considered undersea wilderness scouts.

Most surface dwellers do not know they exist. They keep no allies, and while they have no slave-market value as such, they are occasionally captured and sold.

The book states outright that the Rurlel eel people can be NPCs, villains or optional player characters.
